From 377c528fb1d1c1972b742d9df6c071f852512a67 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jeff Queisser <funkzy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 11:30:00 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 08/58] dt-bindings: spi: apple,qspi: Add t6050

T6050's boot NOR sits behind a QSPIMC controller with the same P and C
apertures (C at P + 0x800) as T8140's. Describe it as
"apple,t6050-qspi", "apple,t8140-qspi" so the driver's T8140 policy (data
reads anywhere, programs and erases only inside the nvram partition)
applies without a driver change.

Signed-off-by: Jeff Queisser <funkzy@users.noreply.github.com>
Signed-off-by: Erik Bourget <erik@ebourget.net>
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/spi/apple,qspi.yaml | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/spi/apple,qspi.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/spi/apple,qspi.yaml
index 40d08a827371..b8472b2df734 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/spi/apple,qspi.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/spi/apple,qspi.yaml
@@ -26,7 +26,9 @@ properties:
           - apple,t6041-qspi
           - apple,t8140-qspi
       - items:
-          - const: apple,t8152-qspi
+          - enum:
+              - apple,t6050-qspi
+              - apple,t8152-qspi
           - const: apple,t8140-qspi
 
   reg:
